=== a pair that refines marks each changed span under its side
    expected  the quick brown fox
                          ~
    actual    the quick brawn fox
                          ~

=== on a terminal, colour marks the changed spans in bold and no ~ line prints
    «d|expected»  the quick br«G|o»wn fox
    «d|actual»    the quick br«R|a»wn fox

=== off a terminal, the ~ lines print under colour too
    «d|expected»  the quick br«G|o»wn fox
                          «G|~»
    «d|actual»    the quick br«R|a»wn fox
                          «R|~»

=== a changed span of spaces keeps its ~ line under colour
    «d|expected»  a long enough «G| »value
                            «G|~»
    «d|actual»    a long enough value

=== a pair the refinement declines prints each side whole
    expected  true
    actual    false

=== and under colour each side whole in its colour
    «d|expected»  «g|true»
    «d|actual»    «r|false»

=== the ~ line counts code points, not bytes
    expected  the café is brown today
                            ~
    actual    the café is brawn today
                            ~

=== a tab on a side: both values, no ~ line
    expected  the	quick brown fox
    actual    the	quick brawn fox

=== a span at the start
    expected  Xbcdefghij
              ~
    actual    Ybcdefghij
              ~

=== a span at the end
    expected  abcdefghiX
                       ~
    actual    abcdefghiY
                       ~

=== a pure insertion is marked under actual only
    expected  user:alice
    actual    user:alice:admin
                        ~~~~~~

=== a pure deletion is marked under expected only
    expected  user:alice:admin
                        ~~~~~~
    actual    user:alice

=== two changed spans on one line
    expected  a1b2c
               ~ ~
    actual    a9b8c
               ~ ~

=== the last code point of fixed width is marked
    expected  ɏabc1
                  ~
    actual    ɏabc2
                  ~

=== one side without fixed widths draws no ~ line
    expected  ab日
    actual    abc

=== a value's escape sequences print as text, an OSC one too
    expected  \x1b[31mred\x1b[0m one
    actual    \x1b]0;title\x07 two

=== a value's control bytes print escaped, the ~ lines under the escapes
    expected  \x1b[31mred\x1b[0m
                    ~
    actual    \x1b[32mred\x1b[0m
                    ~

=== a marked control byte widens its ~ to its four columns
    expected  plain text here
                   ~
    actual    plain\x1btext here
                   ~~~~

=== a deleted control byte is marked under expected, as wide
    expected  plain\x1btext here
                   ~~~~
    actual    plaintext here

=== under colour the changed byte of an escaped value is bold, and the value's own sequence is text
    «d|expected»  \x1b[3«G|1»mred\x1b[0m
    «d|actual»    \x1b[3«R|2»mred\x1b[0m

=== one side elided, coloured, prints each side whole in its colour
    «d|expected»  «g|… (10 bytes elided)»
    «d|actual»    «r|»

=== a ?msg prints above the values
    context note
    expected  1
    actual    2

=== multi-line values are a unified diff under --- expected and +++ actual
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
      a
    - b
    + B
      c

=== a side that spans lines against one that does not
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,2 +1,1 @@
    - a
    - b
    + c

=== a side with no lines
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
    + a
    + b

=== an empty - line answered by a + line
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
      a
    - 
    + x
      c

=== a difference in a trailing newline is said, its side named: actual
    values differ only by a trailing newline (on the actual side)

=== a difference in a trailing newline is said, its side named: expected
    values differ only by a trailing newline (on the expected side)

=== identical renderings print once, then say that the printer shows less
    both sides render as: nan
    the printer shows less than the equality compares

=== identical multi-line renderings print once, indented
    both sides render as:
      line a
      line b
    the printer shows less than the equality compares

=== a - and a + line that differ in a trailing blank: a ~ under the blank
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
    - line one 
              ~
    + line one
      line two

=== an inserted trailing run is marked at its columns
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
    - ab
        ~~
    + ab  
      line two

=== a trailing tab: the ~ line repeats the line's tabs, context keeps its blanks
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
    - a	x	
       	 ~
    + a	x
      common 
      y

=== a visible difference draws no mark
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
    - foo 
    + bar
      line two

=== a run of changes is no pair and draws no mark
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
    - a 
    - b 
    + a
    + b
      z

=== blanks shared past the stem
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
    - x  
        ~
    + x 
      y

=== under colour the trailing blank's ~ is red, outside the line's style
    «d|--- expected»
    «d|+++ actual»
    «d|@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@»
    «g|- line one »
              «r|~»
    «r|+ line one»
      line two

=== under colour a diff's expected lines are green and its actual lines red
    «d|--- expected»
    «d|+++ actual»
    «d|@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@»
      keep
    «g|- expected»
    «r|+ actual»

=== every line of a diff prints escaped
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
      header
    - \x1b[31malert\x1b[0m
    + \x1b[32malert\x1b[0m
      footer

=== a carriage return prints as its escape
    --- expected
    +++ actual
    @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
      one
    - two\x0d
    + two
      three

=== a claim takes the expected side and is never refined
    expected  value satisfying the predicate
    actual    -3

=== a multi-line value against a claim prints as a block
    expected  value satisfying the predicate
    actual:
      [0; 1;
       2]

=== under colour each line of that block is red, no style spans two
    «d|expected»  «g|value satisfying the predicate»
    «d|actual:»
      «r|[0; 1;»
      «r| 2]»

=== a match's claim is not refined either
    expected  a match
    actual    Error "boom"

=== every C0 byte and DEL print as \xNN
    expected  a clean value
    actual    a\x00b\x07c\x0dd\x7fe\x1ff

=== TAB stays inside a line and LF breaks the block
    expected  a clean value
    actual:
      one	two
      three

=== two single-line sides cut to the same kept bytes say what they agree on
    the sides agree on the 65536 bytes a failure keeps of each (expected 65537 bytes, actual 65537 bytes)

=== so do two multi-line sides
    the sides agree on the 65536 bytes a failure keeps of each (expected 88001 bytes, actual 88001 bytes)
